urns 503 twice, then 200.\n`WeatherClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries on HTTP 503, up to 3 attempts in total.\n\n- **Backoff:** it sleeps 0.5s after the first 503 and 1s after the second, so the delay doubles each time.\n- **Giving up:** if all 3 attempts return 503, the final `HTTPError` is raised. Any other HTTP error is raised immediately with no retry.\n- **Constructor options:** `__init__` takes two new keyword arguments, `attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`. Existing callers don't need to change.\n\nI checked it against a local test server:\n\n| Server behavior | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503 twice, then 200 | Returned the JSON | 3 |\n| Always 503 | Raised a 503 error | 3 |\n| 200 straight away | Returned the JSON | 1 |\n\nI only ran that one-off check; I didn't add a test file to the repo.\n\nOnly HTTP 503 is retried. Network failures such as timeouts or refused connections are not.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35278, "requests_cache_write": 142038, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3733868, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1474, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial27", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 113, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T00:47:18.799382+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 15.915, "t_checker_s": 1.886, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1486, "tokens_cache_read": 35278, "tokens_cache_write": 142038, 